<title>UKRAINE: Ukraine wage backlog grows to almost $2 bln-c.bank.</title>
<headline>Ukraine wage backlog grows to almost $2 bln-c.bank.</headline>
<dateline>KIEV 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ukraine's wage backlog owed to government workers, pensioners and students has reached nearly $2 billion, the central bank chairman said late on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The wage bill was 3.625 billion hryvnia as of December 6,&quot; Viktor Yushchenko said at a news conference.</p>
<p>The government has promised to clear the debt next year, which increased from about $1.5 billion in the summer.</p>
<p>The draft budget, currently before parliament and expected to be passed early next year, makes provision to pay the money.</p>
<p>About 200,000 miners, unpaid for months, went on strike during the summer to demand back pay, and teachers have also held nation-wide protests.</p>
<p>--Irene Marushko, Kiev Newsroom +380 44 229 2264</p>
